\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Fanbak (Fanbyak, Orkon; ISO 639-3 \texttt{fnb}) is an endangered Austronesian language of northern Ambrym, Vanuatu. Speaker estimates range from about 95 to about 130. The village of Fanbyak is abandoned and speakers live mainly among North Ambrym speakers. Whether the Orkon variety was a separate lect is unsettled.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No school materials were found in search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia article on the Fanbak language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fanbak_language}
\item Culture in Crisis project page, ``A Documentation of Orkon/Fanbak, a language of Vanuatu'': \url{https://cultureincrisis.org/projects/a-documentation-of-orkon-fanbak-a-language-of-vanuatu}
\item Glottolog / TLOPO records: \url{https://tlopo.clld.org/languages/orkon}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item ELDP collection ``The languages of Northern Ambrym, Vanuatu'' (documentation archive; per search summary, grammar sketch, texts and sociolinguistic study deposited with ELAR): \url{https://eldp.access.preservica.com/dk01310387/}
\item University of Surrey dataset for the northern Ambrym languages: \url{https://openresearch.surrey.ac.uk/esploro/outputs/dataset/Data-for-The-languages-of-northern/99862365502346}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The language is documented by researchers but not taught. A curriculum would depend on community consultation and on the archived documentation, whose access conditions were not checked.

\end{document}
